  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on its first run, so I used 1 of the 6 allowed runs. It reported 3 witnesses, 1 name and 1 atom read.\n\n**Concept file** (`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/motion/stopping_distance.lean`): the body computes `speed·reaction_time + (speed·speed) / (2·deceleration)`.\n- Speed comes from `kin_speed` of `x`.\n- The `2` is the record's declared literal, written as `Units.ratio 2 1`.\n- The divisor uses only the `deceleration` parameter and that literal, never a measured value, so the language allows the division.\n- The value is unknown when the speed isn't observed, and zero for a car at a standstill.\n- The contract states the formula exactly, so I declared no narrowings.\n\n**Witness file** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/motion/stopping_distance.lean`): the instance sets a reaction time of 1 s, a deceleration of 5 m/s² and expected bounds of 19–21 m. Each scenario has one car driving east at a steady speed, observed three times one second apart.\n\n| Scenario | Speed | Distance | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `holds` | 10 m/s | 20 m, inside the bounds | compliant |\n| `fails` | 20 m/s | 60 m, above 21 m | violated |\n| `blind` | as `holds`, speed not observed | unknown | unknown |\n\nIn `blind`, the speed is both masked in the manifest and left empty in the scenes.\n\n`task_result.md` in the working directory records the verdict, the single gate run and these choices.",
